<ArticleLayout
  title="GarageCloud vs Dragon2000 | Comparison"
  description="How GarageCloud compares to Dragon2000 (DragonDMS): pricing and who each is built for. Dragon2000 is aimed primarily at car dealerships; GarageCloud is built for independent workshops and trades."
  eyebrow="Comparison"
  breadcrumbLabel="GarageCloud vs Dragon2000"
  heading="GarageCloud vs Dragon2000"
  lede="Dragon2000's DragonDMS is built primarily for car dealerships. GarageCloud is built for independent garages and the trades around them."
>
  <p>
    <strong>Dragon2000 and GarageCloud are aimed at different businesses.</strong> Dragon2000's DragonDMS has been
    in the UK market for over 30 years and serves more than 1,000 vehicle businesses, but its primary market is car
    dealerships — it includes used-car stock management, dealer website integration and finance product
    administration alongside workshop tools
    (see <a href="https://www.dragon2000.co.uk/garage-software/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Dragon2000's own product page</a>).
    GarageCloud is built for independent garages, MOT centres, mobile fitters, locksmiths and fleet services —
    without the dealership-specific tooling.
  </p>

  <h2>Pricing</h2>
  <p>
    Dragon2000's published pricing is £99.95 per user, per month. GarageCloud's Starter plan is £50/month excluding
    VAT with unlimited staff included, rather than a per-user rate.
  </p>

  <h2>What Dragon2000 does well</h2>
  <p>
    DragonDMS offers both cloud-hosted and Windows desktop options, which suits a workshop with inconsistent
    internet or older infrastructure. Its interactive condition reports, colour-coded booking diary, and online
    card payment links are mature, well-built features backed by three decades in the market — and its dealership
    tooling (stock, finance admin, dealer website) is a genuine strength if that's the business.
  </p>

  <h2>Where GarageCloud is different, not necessarily better</h2>
  <p>
    GarageCloud is pre-launch and doesn't have Dragon2000's dealership feature set — nor is it trying to. If a
    business is a car dealership needing stock and finance administration alongside workshop tools, Dragon2000 is
    built for that. If it's an independent garage, mobile trade, or fleet service that doesn't need dealership
    tooling, GarageCloud's Starter plan is priced and built for that instead.
  </p>
</ArticleLayout>
